Patch: 017-mcp-servers
Reason: TEST-ONLY. It changes only the vendored stand-in for app-server, test/fake-app-server.mjs (6 lines: an import, the `mcp`/`outputs` turn and the thread/start check), to hook in test/fake-app-server-mcp.js, a file of ours that plays Codex's own MCP client in tests (tools/call with its call id in _meta.callId, and a required server that does not start failing thread/start). The real Codex 0.164 needs no patch: the session's machine writes mcp_servers into Codex's config.toml, at the session proxy's /mcp/<server>, and Codex's own client calls that door.
Upstream: ours
Pins: codex: an agent granted mcp:fake/add calls it through the session's proxy; the timeline reads fake · add, the fake saw the bearer, no file holds it
Pins: codex: a run killed mid-call resumes with the call answered interrupted, and the server saw the call once
